      "properties": {},
      "title": "Read me first",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 11 · The Film Director\n\nOne script, a whole film. **VIG H3 Film Director** splits it into beats, fixes\nthe **cast and the places once** for the whole film, and writes each beat's H3\nprompt knowing what came before — then hands the Cutter the lot through its\nlast socket. Without it, every clip is written on its own, and a character\ndescribed twice in different words is rendered as two different people.\n\n**Your divisions are kept.** Blank lines or a numbered list are read as your\nbeats; plain prose is split about two sentences to a beat. `total_seconds` of 0\nmeans \"as long as the story needs\".\n\n**Press Run twice.** The first run plans the film and lays the timeline out;\nthe second renders it. A storyboard is applied once: pressing Run again never\nlays the plan back over clips you have edited since. For another take of the\nsame story, change `writer_seed`.\n\n**From footage.** Point `video` at a file in ComfyUI's input folder and a\nvision model describes it; that becomes the script.\n\nYou can skip the writer entirely: the **VIG H3 Storyboard (JSON)** node takes a\nfinished storyboard with every prompt already written."
      ]
    },
